  unit: { count: 41, covers: "The verdicts that read the probes beside them. The not-decrypting remedy defers to a certificate probe that reads trusted and sends no one back to the certificate step, and a trusted certificate changes no other traffic reading's words (R18). The end credits this machine only for trust trusted and proxy ours, across seven probe pairs (R17). The reversal's line names the certificate only where it reads trusted (R14). Round 8's evidence: nothing yet is no evidence; any request that reached Trawler shows the route however long ago; a tunnel inside its grace is not a refusal and one past it with nothing decrypted is, and stays one; one decrypted request outranks a later refusal; a tunnel answered by a later decrypt is not unanswered. A task no probe concludes reads its evidence (decrypted done, refused not done, nothing a promise naming the first HTTPS request), a concluding probe is never overruled by traffic (DEC-33), the route reads done on any request reaching Trawler, the certificate task's refusal names whose store and points at its steps, and the try task leaves a refusal to a certificate task that is not done. The existing verdict tests still run beside them." }
  integration: { count: 173, covers: "The screen's contract at render. Onboarding: each task holds its own route under the one act, which leads task 1, and nothing renders between tasks. On macOS and Windows, the four readings: P8 inverted (certificate trusted, proxy off gives no one act, the proxy task's own action and steps, no certificate install step anywhere); the mirror opens the certificate's steps in task 1 with the reversal in task 2; both done leaves no install step or action and each way back shut. A failed set-up, set-proxy or unset opens the route its note names, a dismissed prompt opens nothing, and the button's line stays above what happened. The reversal sits in task 2, on the Simulator too, appears on resolve before the re-read, and comes back when the proxy is set again after it was taken off. The end names no device while a probe reads not done; the remedy defers to a trusted certificate. The owner's iPhone case: requests that arrive and do not decrypt read the proxy task done and folded to its way back, the certificate task not done with the refusal and its steps open, and the try task with its state line only; on this machine the refusal is said in task 1 with its steps open. The permanent state matrix: host (4) x all eight platforms x reach armed or not x trust (3) x proxy (4) x eight traffic histories at rest, and every offered action in every outcome - 6577 states - each flattened to an outline and judged against a reading model written independently of the screen (the certificate and proxy task states, where a refusal is said, every sentence pointing at the steps below has them open, a done task keeps only its way back, place and time of every action). 2984 of them are red against the screen before round 8, and the first sweep's 2017 had 340 red against the pre-WU screen. App: a real set-up failure leaves task 1's route open with the OS's words, the save step is reached through task 1's route, and a connection no request answers is said in the certificate task once its grace is spent." }
  e2e: { waived: "Waived at WU level as the epic plan rules for R12: the per-half layout turns on the real machine's trust store and proxy, which a hermetic run cannot set, so the readings are pinned at Onboarding level and in the matrix. The walkthrough was re-run through the real Tauri window as evidence: green at c114629 with 24 reels and 144 chapters, the R12-R18 chapters showing the new layout. The epic's e2e is W6's." }
